[B] what coprimality means, checked exhaustively for 2<=p<=400, 1<=q<p
    lemma: the first p glyphs k*q mod p (k=0..p-1) are all distinct <=> gcd(p,q)=1
    and the number of distinct positions is p/gcd(p,q)
  lemma counterexamples over 79800 (p,q) pairs               record=0              mine=0              MATCH
    torus-link note: the gcd(p,q) components of the (p,q) torus link are the level
    sets q*x - p*y = c/d (mod 1), c = 0..d-1, which are pairwise disjoint; so on the
    torus gcd>1 gives several parallel strands that still never touch each other.
